.TH USERADD 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
useradd \- create a new user account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B useradd
.RB [ \-d
.IR home ]
.RB [ \-s
.IR shell ]
.I username
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create
.I username
in
.BR /etc/passwd " and " /etc/shadow ,
with a freshly allocated UID, a new matching private group of the
same name, and a home directory (mode 0700, owned by the new user;
default
.BR /home/ username ).
The account's password starts
.B locked
(a literal
.B !
in
.BR /etc/shadow ) --
run
.BR "passwd " username
separately to actually set one.
.SH DELIBERATELY NARROWER THAN REAL USERADD
No
.B /etc/skel
copying, no
.B \-G
(supplementary groups at creation time), no system-account
.RB ( \-r )
support.
.SH SECURITY
.B This has not been independently security-reviewed.
Modifies
.BR /etc/passwd ", " /etc/shadow ", and " /etc/group
directly, under the same lock file real shadow-utils uses. Read
.B common::accounts
in the source before installing this setuid anywhere that matters --
the same weight as
.BR su (1)/ sudo (1)'s
own SECURITY sections. Get it reviewed and test it in a disposable
VM first.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR and \fB\-\-version\fR, and \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the account already exists, the name is
invalid, or the database couldn't be locked/written.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR passwd (1),
.BR groupadd (1),
.BR mitos\-box (1)
